<div class="settings-page">
  <header class="top-bar">
    <a href="javascript:history.back()" class="back-link" aria-label="Back">←</a>
    <h2 class="settings-title">Privacy</h2>
  </header>

  <h5 class="mt-3">What Bloom stores</h5>
  <ul>
    <li>Your username and password. The password is stored scrambled (hashed), so no one can read it.</li>
    <li>Your recovery email, if you add one. It's used only to send password reset links.</li>
    <li>The plants you save: the photo, where you found it, and when.</li>
    <li>Your points and badges.</li>
  </ul>

  <h5>Your photos</h5>
  <p>
    When you identify a plant, the photo is sent to Pl@ntNet so it can recognize the plant.
    Bloom doesn't show your photos or your Bloomdex to other users.
  </p>

  <h5>Your choices</h5>
  <ul>
    <li>Change your username, recovery email, or password in <a href="/settings/account">Account</a>.</li>
    <li>Remove a plant with "Remove from Bloomdex" on its page.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
